<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch bonds end higher but rate hike talk persists.</title>
<headline>Dutch bonds end higher but rate hike talk persists.</headline>
<text>
<p>---------------------(Snapshot at 1545 GMT)---------------------</p>
<p>* DUTCH STATE LOANS	 PRICES			  BID YIELDS</p>
<p>  June 1999 7.50 pct	106.36/46 (-0.02)	   3.90 (+0.01)</p>
<p>  Feb  2002		   114.56/66 (+0.08)	   4.61 (-0.01)</p>
<p>  Feb  2007 5.75 pct	101.98/08 (+0.17)	   5.47 (-0.02)</p>
<p>  Jan  2023		   116.72/92 (+0.39)	   6.17 (-0.03)</p>
<p>* BUND FUTURE (Sept)	103.15 (+0.30)</p>
<p>  TREASURIES  (Sept)	115.65 (+0.49 vs pvs Dutch close)</p>
<p>* DM/NLG			1.1269 (prev 1.1266)</p>
<p>--------------------------(SPREADS)----------------------------</p>
<p>*DSLs versus Bunds  (pvs close)    *DSL curve     (pvs close)</p>
<p> 5 yr	 +0.04	LEVEL	  10-2 yr  158     (159)</p>
<p> 10 yr	-0.05	-0.06	  10-5 yr   87	(87)</p>
<p> Long	 -0.04	-0.05</p>
<p>--------------------------(July 29)----------------------------</p>
<p>* Dutch bonds end firmer, short end the exception as talk persists of Dutch rate hike on Thurs to prop up weak guilder.</p>
<p>* U.S. Q2 ECI as expected, market looking ahead to U.S. July non-farm payrolls on Friday. Little else of interest as summer holidays depresses trading levels.</p>
